[Unit]
Description=KiCraft build-slot leak sweep (reclaim host build slots held by orphaned builds)
# A SIGKILLed campaign orphans its build child, and the build timeout lives in the *parent*, so
# the orphan is unbounded: if it is blocked rather than dead it keeps the flock on a host build
# slot forever. Measured 2026-09-19 on this box: an orphaned `cli_app build` held slot_0 for
# 12 h 24 m at 1 s CPU / 407 MB while the build worker — which sizes its concurrency from the same
# host gate — ran on one slot instead of two. Nothing else notices, because a leaked slot is
# silent: the next build simply takes another slot and looks healthy.
#
# The sweep only matches orphaned (ppid 1) build/route command lines, so the detached services
# (kicraft.server.web and kicraft.server.build_worker are ppid 1 by design) are never touched, and
# --min-age-s (120 s) leaves a restart's in-flight orphans time to exit on their own.

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=kicraft
Environment=KICRAFT_BUILD_SLOTS_MONITOR_LOG=/home/kicraft/KiCraft/logs/build_slots_monitor.log
ExecStart=/bin/bash -c 'exec /home/kicraft/KiCraft/deploy/check-build-slots.sh --reap >> "$KICRAFT_BUILD_SLOTS_MONITOR_LOG" 2>&1'
TimeoutStartSec=120
